<title>USA: EchoStar says News Corp deal to proceed.</title>
<headline>EchoStar says News Corp deal to proceed.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>EchoStar Communications Corp said Friday it expects its $1 billion satellite venture with News Corp Ltd to &quot;proceed in accordance with the agreement.&quot;</p>
<p>EchoStar said it was making the statement in response to a report in the newspaper USA Today that said News Corp might be looking at Primestar as an alternative partner.</p>
<p>Primestar is a satellite company comtrolled by Tele-Communications Inc, Time Warner Inc, U S West Inc, Comcast Corp and Cox Communications Inc.  </p>
<p>EchoStar said, &quot;As previously announced, the company has a binding agreement with the News Corp Ltd. Discussions, such as those described in the USA Today article, would be inconsistent with that agreement.&quot;</p>
</text>
